Player base speed is 12; for the player, "fast" is 16 and "very fast" is
20.  After hasting, a gnomish wizard or gnome king (base speed 10) will
be 16.67% faster (speed 14) than you (on average), but a gnome lord (base
speed 8) will remain 8.33% slower than you (speed 11) and a gnome (base
speed 6) will be 33.33% slower (speed 8) than you, if you are at normal
speed and unburdened.  If you are at least fast and are not Burdened or
worse, you are faster than any gnome, even a hasted one.

Furthermore, *all* monster dwarves have base speed 6, so even a dwarf
king will never catch a fleeing player unless said player gets cornered
or sandwiched.
